#: ../../start/first-look.rst:2 753384057b4f436abf56194c7813f7fe
msgid "A first look"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:4 b68aead0584f44f4a8e3bbbb56161130
msgid ""
"This walks through opening the console for the first time and checking "
"that MHVTL underneath it is running. Installing it is in the *Guides* - "
"*Installation*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:13 3d06d45b115a419c9064c419ae689f76
msgid "Log in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:15 12760faecb2042619b7838965d3f5ef8
msgid ""
"Open ``https://your-server/``. The certificate the installer creates is "
"self-signed, so a browser asks about it once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:18 7c6c9af658a14c778fae498ec01273a2
msgid ""
"There is one password for the whole console, and it starts as ``mhvtl``. "
"While it is still that, every page carries a warning saying so, with a "
"link that changes it. See :doc:`../running/password`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:22 4809be6f31064657995baab6d8771344
msgid "``http://your-server/`` redirects to the HTTPS address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:26 e41197e6499d46c183148ece9757e462
msgid ""
"If something else on the host already uses port 80 or 443 - another web "
"application, a reverse proxy - the installer's nginx configuration will "
"not start beside it, and whoever installed it will have moved the console"
" to another port, usually 8443 with 8080 redirecting. Then the address is"
" ``https://your-server:8443/``. *Installation* in the *Guides* has the "
"two lines to change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:34 ad42cef41e83426f958390c4b70bf679
msgid "Is MHVTL running?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:36 5db9f9f3bfd74de6a6ba7dff7715d6b6
msgid ""
"The console is a window onto MHVTL, so if MHVTL is not running there is "
"nothing to see. **Console → Services** answers it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:48 edf2533308954157947dca58f504db33
msgid "If the target is not active:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:55 3b63452bef0446c7aeec17072ba1e8a6
msgid "What you see first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:57 7455b1eb807a40ff8eea45df2afa13b3
msgid ""
"**Dashboard** is the overview: how many libraries, how many are running, "
"what the host is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:60 8550bf5498154881885af6395d8039c5
msgid "The dashboard: libraries, their state, and the host"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:64 6e14ef83c7424290a3b95c803eed2f7d
msgid ""
"**Libraries** lists every library MHVTL has, read from its configuration "
"rather than from the console's own records - so a library somebody "
"created from the command line a minute ago is in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:68 628b5688c7224816be4095ed12bac78f
msgid "The Libraries page, listing four libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:72 5e1ac07464d24794b0d12dd133b668c5
msgid ""
"Click one and you are on :doc:`../libraries/the-library-page`, which is "
"where most work happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:76 098a50aaaa96491998c4bb82ce433bc9
msgid "The same thing from the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:88 c1386f38537b44b79c10a69a4a44dd16
msgid ""
"``mhvtl`` reads the same configuration the console does and needs no web "
"server running. Everything in this guide can be done either way; each "
"page shows both."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:93 1ac11fd66c0a4f30bc343cfba0fbbd50
msgid "If there are no libraries yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start/first-look.rst:95 7ed3b96bea2041c1b06bd32ee28fd55e
msgid ""
"That is the ordinary state after installing. Go to "
":doc:`../libraries/create`."
msgstr ""

